(6) SPIN V/S Pace

season	pace_economy	spin_economy
2026	   9.49	            8.61
2025	   9.53	            8.43
2024	   8.68	            7.88
2023	   8.62	            7.63
2022	   8.55	            7.28
2021	   8.35	            6.58
2020	   7.98	            8.40
2019	   7.85          	6.77
2018	   8.42	            8.26


observations: 

Spin bowling consistently outperformed pace bowling in most successful CSK seasons.

The strongest seasons (2019, 2021 and 2023) recorded excellent spin economy rates below 8 runs per over.

However, recent seasons have seen a sharp increase in spin economy, rising from 6.58 in 2021 to 8.61 in 2026.

This suggests that CSK's traditional strength of controlling the game through spin may have weakened significantly.


conclusion:


Bowling efficiency, particularly spin bowling efficiency, appears to have a stronger relationship with team success than most batting metrics analysed earlier.

Strong CSK teams were able to restrict scoring through both pace and spin, while weaker teams struggled to maintain economical bowling attacks.

The deterioration of spin economy in recent seasons may be one of the major factors contributing to CSK's decline.


